# The docs/ vault commits only what makes it the same from any checkout: which
# community plugins are on, BRAT's list (so BRAT installs review-md on a fresh
# clone) and review-md's reviewer name. Plugin code, window layout and caches stay
# local. Plan: ../catalog/plan.md, "review-md".
#
# BRAT's data.json has a token field. It is empty: BRAT 2.x keeps tokens in
# Obsidian's secret store instead. Never paste a token there; gitleaks would
# block the commit.
#
# Also local on purpose: graph.json (Obsidian rewrites it every time the graph
# view moves; `tools/vault_audit.py --setup-graph` merges our color groups into
# it) and core-plugins.json (Bases, Properties, Graph and Backlinks are core
# plugins; the audit reports any that are off on this machine). The views
# themselves are notes, docs/bases/*.base, and are committed like any note.
# Rules: ../../.claude/skills/vault-setup/vault-rules.md
/*
!/.gitignore
!/app.json
!/community-plugins.json
!/plugins/
/plugins/*/*
!/plugins/obsidian42-brat/data.json
!/plugins/review-md/data.json
